  (footprint "temper:CMC_B82726S" (version 20231120) (generator temper-hand) (layer "F.Cu")
    (tedit e6707f3f) (tstamp 594c12ff-3567-99f8-0482-cc86e20c7af9)
    (at 65.0 63.0)
    (descr "TDK (EPCOS) B82726S2163N030 current-compensated ring-core double choke, 250VAC/16A, 2.2mH/winding. Land pattern hand-built from the official TDK dimensional drawing (tdk-electronics.tdk.com/inf/30/db/ind_2008/b82726s2163.pdf, page 3 'Dimensional drawing and pin configuration', April 2025 revision): pin 1/2 (top row) on 18+/-0.4mm pitch, pin 4/3 (bottom row) on 38+/-0.3mm pitch, row-to-row (1/2 row to 4/3 row) pitch 23+/-0.2mm, lead diameter 1.6+/-0.1mm. Body envelope from the dimensional drawing (plan + elevation): vertical toroid 50mm max wide x 49mm max tall, plan-view ring strip 16.5+/-0.4mm deep, polycarbonate base plate spanning the pin field (rows 23+/-0.2mm apart). Courtyard is the real rectangular envelope (50mm width, pin field + base edge depth) + 0.5mm clearance per IPC-7351 -- tightened 2026-07-16 from the earlier conservative 54mm circle. PAD NUMBERING matches TDK's own pin numbers 1-4 (no remapping): footprint pads 1-4 = atopile CommonModeChoke pins 1-4 directly (winding 1 = pads 1+4, winding 2 = pads 2+3). Datasheet states 'No polarity' -- the two windings are symmetric so there is no dot/phasing convention to respect.")
